course: dictionary
lesson: 2187
title: Costly: high price or big loss
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Costly is an adjective, and it has two meanings. The sentence tells you which one to use. Costly means costing a lot of money, like something expensive. «Bird's nest soup» is an expensive food, and its nests are costly because they must be collected very carefully.
explain: The second meaning is causing a big loss or harm. «A costly mistake» is one that makes you lose something important, like a match or a prize. Ask yourself: is the sentence about money, or about what was lost? That question tells you which meaning fits.
explain: You can check with a swap. Put expensive in place of costly. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the money meaning. If it does not, try loss or harm, as in «a costly mistake».
fact: Costly means costing a lot of money; expensive.
fact: Costly can also mean causing a big loss or harm, as in «a costly mistake».
fact: The comparative and superlative forms are costlier and costliest.
fact: «Prove costly» means that something turns out to cost you a lot in the end.
fact: In the West, silk was rare and costly because China kept the making of silk secret for a long time.
exercise: «The nests are costly because they must be collected carefully from cave walls.» What does costly mean here? | *Costing a lot of money, expensive | Very loud and noisy | Fun to collect | Easy to find on every wall
exercise: Sam made «a costly mistake» in the final, and his team lost. What does costly mean here? | *Causing a big loss or harm | Funny and light | Cheap and easy to buy | Very loud
exercise: Find and copy the one word in this sentence that means expensive: «Silk was rare and costly in the West.» | *costly | West | silk | rare
test: «Space missions are hugely hard and costly, and their dates very often slip.» What does costly mean here? | *Costing a lot of money | Happy and bright | Quick and simple
test: Which word is the comparative form of costly, meaning more costly? | costlyer | costliest | cost | *costlier
exam: Ella says costly means cheap. Who is right? | Ella, it means cheap | Ella, it means happy | Ella, it means very quiet | *Nobody, costly means costing a lot or causing a big loss
